    ★ RATIO       = guest GFLOP/s ÷ native GFLOP/s, from the per-launch MEDIAN (steady
                    state, first launch discarded). THIS IS THE HEADLINE.
    ★ BATCHRAT    = the same ratio from the BATCHED per-launch cost (K launches, ONE
                    sync). BATCHRAT >> RATIO ⇒ the cost is in the per-launch SUBMIT/
                    COMPLETION round trip and an LLM could amortise it. BATCHRAT ≈ RATIO
                    ⇒ the cost is in the ENGINE or the work itself and batching will not
                    help.

=== ★★★ ABSOLUTE OVERHEAD PER LAUNCH — the (D)/(E) discriminator
    ⊘ A RATIO CANNOT TELL (D) FROM (E). If the guest is a constant FACTOR slower the
      ratio is flat and the ABSOLUTE gap grows with N; if the guest pays a fixed
      NUMBER OF MILLISECONDS per launch the ratio IMPROVES with N while the gap stays
      flat. Those two have opposite implications for an LLM, so the gap is printed.
